//! Types moved out of `iyakki_agent::voiceassisttools` (F-SPLIT-03, scripted by dist/split/move_types.py); the agent re-exports them.



pub const PROMPT_RULE: &str = "\nMY IYAKKI (voice assistant): voice_assistant_status says whether the push-to-talk voice assistant is on, muted, and its follow-up window (Voice tile -> Assistant tab). voice_assistant_set (on, muted, wake, follow_up_seconds 0 to 20) changes it; voice_wake_status says whether the experimental, opt-in wake phrase \"My IYAKKI\" has a model and whether anything listens for it. voice_assistant_set with wake=true (needs a trained model file; wake_sensitivity low, normal or high) always asks the person, and only a tap or key approves it, never a spoken yes. With the wake phrase on, the microphone listens on every screen (a red sign shows while it does) but sound stays in memory and is never recorded or sent. Otherwise the microphone is only open while the Voice tile shows it. voice_wake_stats says how often the wake phrase was heard, dropped by the experimental second check (voice_assistant_set wake_confirm, off by default), marked wrong or marked missed; voice_wake_mark (kind false_wake or miss) counts one mistake the person reports and asks. voice_backends lists the speech-to-text backends (set up or not, where the sound goes, whether they ask for consent) without keys; voice_session_settings_status says whether spoken approvals are on (off by default) and voice_session_settings_set (spoken_approvals true or false) changes it: it always asks, and a tap or key approves it. Whatever that setting says, the hard-ask list can only be approved by a tap or a key, never by voice.";
